{"title":"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Quick_Solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Quick Solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many unordered pairs of edges of a given cube determine a plane?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/6/d46b2aea68248c7549a772340af1923cddc34a12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 12 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 28 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 36\\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 42 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"398\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Without loss of generality, choose one of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> edges of the cube to be among the two selected. We now calculate the probability that a randomly-selected second edge makes the pair satisfy the condition in the problem statement.\n</p><p>For two lines in space to determine a common plane, they must either intersect or be parallel (in other words, they cannot be skew lines). If all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> line segments are extended to lines, the first (arbitrarily chosen) edge's line intersects <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> lines and is parallel to another <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/916792d3166c88332e80557114630afd438626b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4+3=7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572ac27aab1a8abd8d9b533fafc987065820636b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12-1=11$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"90\" height=\"12\" /> remaining line segments (which could be chosen for the second edge) give a pair of lines determining a common plane. To see this, observe that in the diagram below, the red edge is parallel to the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> green edges and intersects with the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> blue edges.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/2/7d2fb38c071febb9479738c42fa5468680d9496e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import three; import three; unitsize(1cm); size(200); currentprojection=perspective(-6/5,-8/5,7/8); draw((0,1,0)--(0,0,0)--(1,0,0), blue); draw((1,0,0)--(1,1,0)--(0,1,0)); draw((0,0,0)--(0,0,1), red); draw((0,1,0)--(0,1,1), green); draw((1,1,0)--(1,1,1), green); draw((1,0,0)--(1,0,1), green); draw((0,1,1)--(0,0,1)--(1,0,1), blue); draw((1,0,1)--(1,1,1)--(0,1,1)); [/asy]\" width=\"335\" height=\"302\" />\n</p><p>This means that the probability that a randomly-selected pair of edges determine a plane is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/d/86d2ae99ef937044429b0550afe4a0baf2db28a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{11}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, and we calculate that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f363e54394035b19d42157360920421dd1f88b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${12 \\choose 2} = 66$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"88\" height=\"53\" /> total pairs of edges that could be chosen (without the restriction). Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/7/d479c8f69b93cb6634c1c7506611769d4bfa2f75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{7}{11} \\cdot 66 =\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }42}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"143\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in Solution 1, we observe that the two edges must either be parallel or intersect. Clearly the edges will intersect if and only if they are part of the same face. We can thus divide into two cases:\n</p><p><b>Case 1</b>: The two edges are part of the same face. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> faces, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/5/c555de232a89fb53ada2f2bd60b778610fe08d53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${4 \\choose 2}=6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"70\" height=\"53\" /> ways to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> edges of the square, giving a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/9/999956907865d13963bffca0c70fb57df8f1f734.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\cdot 6 = 36$\" width=\"73\" height=\"12\" /> possibilities.\n</p><p><b>Case 2</b>: The two edges are parallel and not part of the same face. Observe that each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> edges is parallel to exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> edge that is not part of its face. The edges can thus be paired up, giving <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec956e0ab38c40e4aab6db21bffdfd13e2d1719.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{12}{2} = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"55\" height=\"37\" /> possibilities for this case.\n</p><p>Adding the two cases, the answer is hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/6/7665c99f159f2b3b7b261ce106e420b7a1027348.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36 + 6 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }42}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"139\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Quick_Solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Quick_Solution)\">Solution 3 (Quick Solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Quick Solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>As in solution 1, we see that for an arbitrary edge of the cube, only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> of the other edges can be chosen to form a plane.\n</p><p>For each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> edges, this gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/8/8488389a9af16588ab8189a7bc8cb65f5b91b880.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(7)(12) = 84$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"100\" height=\"20\" /> total possible pairings. However each pair has been counted twice (e.g edge <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and edge <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />) so we divide by 2 to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/1/961575c1932433407c5646345fae6dcc879ec0aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }42}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B\">2019 AMC 12B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_4\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_5\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_6\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_7\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_15\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_19\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_20\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_23\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2019 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017190446\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.052 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 250/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2298/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 158/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5771/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.601      1 -total\n 58.81%    7.411      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 39.50%    4.977      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17321:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017190446 and revision id 134728. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}